{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:c285787da26dc6dd","name":"Raik Muun","source":{"id":"source:reference-c285787da26dc6dd","title":"Raik Muun","revision":21721,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T02:21:14Z","sha256":"dca90daa432b93cc122f258e7bbc208843efde88b2017f0930cb6ae640654613","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21721","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Raik%20Muun&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-c285787da26dc6dd","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dawn of Defiance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dawn_of_Defiance"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Echoes of the Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Echoes_of_the_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:e6a2e80208e1e351"},")"]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Inquisitorius"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Inquisitorius","referenceId":"reference:322ca1aa843ce214"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["The fire-haired woman stalks toward you, clad in a dark version of the Inquisitor's attire. She appears ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"},", but something about her says otherwise. Then you see it. Draco's gaze shows ruthlessness and calculation, but this Dark Jedi's entrancing, green-slitted pupils harbor only murder and dementia."]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["With the flick of a thumb, the red blade of her ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," streaks into existence, casting her body into a bewitching vermilion glow. Each syllable of her death sentence tumbles like wisps of smoke from her lips."]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["\"Come at me one at a time or all at once. All shall pass from this world.\""]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A former Padawan at ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Almas Academy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Almas_Academy"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"}," half-breed Raik Muun once fell in love with a fellow Jedi student. When her affections were not reciprocated, love turned to obsession, and Master ",{"tag":"a","children":["Kirlocca"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Kirlocca?action=edit&redlink=1"}," dismissed her from the academy. Angered at these rejections, Raik became bent on revenge. She attempted to undermine ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"}," by impersonating members of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi Order"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi_Order"}," while publicly performing acts of sabotage and chaos. Muun also learned of the existence of an evil creature called a ",{"tag":"a","children":["T'salak"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/T%27salak","referenceId":"reference:04f3fcf5598f0786"},", and by kidnapping and impersonating a Jedi, she gained possession of the beast. Successfully fissioning the creature into multiple entities, she attempted to use two ",{"tag":"a","children":["T'salaks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/T%27salaks?action=edit&redlink=1"}," to turn some Jedi into crazed killers during a peace conference. Her plan failed, but Master ",{"tag":"a","children":["Kirlocca"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Kirlocca?action=edit&redlink=1"}," lost his life defeating the ",{"tag":"a","children":["T'salaks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/T%27salaks?action=edit&redlink=1"},", and Raik escaped.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["When Raik returned to her base on the planet ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tilnes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tilnes"},", she learned about the decimation of Jedi throughout the galaxy as a result of Order 66. Her revenge was now denied, but she could still fuel the rumors of the \"Jedi Rebellion.\" Raik went to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Coruscant"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Coruscant","referenceId":"reference:2ee37a21e9e7a955"}," to confront those responsible for the destruction of the self-righteous Force-users, not sure if she should thank them or kill them. That's when she met Inquisitor ",{"tag":"a","children":["Valin Draco"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Valin_Draco","referenceId":"reference:225b744e6f6a9bf6"},". The Inquisitor saw enormous potential in the wild-eyed Dark Jedi and asked her to join him. Raik felt that she had finally found someone who would love her back.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Raik has accompanied Draco on various assignments, indulging in the opportunity to hunt Jedi. When Draco travels to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Almas"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Almas","referenceId":"reference:11673f48c5b0ad05"},", Raik's familiarity with the academy proves essential, as does the ",{"tag":"a","children":["T'salak"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/T%27salak","referenceId":"reference:04f3fcf5598f0786"}," she brought along.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Raik Muun Statistics (CL 6)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Near-Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Near-Human","referenceId":"reference:9e3b9745aa61a48a"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi","referenceId":"reference:0b0e48747027a29d"}," 6\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 